{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero","id":571205,"title":"Compact: Llannerch Athrawon - The Wizard Behind the Hero","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-28T05:24:56-07:00","id":571205,"title":"Compact: Llannerch Athrawon - The Wizard Behind the Hero","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/2TzGQLS.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <div align=\"center\">Art by Reaper Verse</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>\u201cRecognise her?\u201d </i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cI think it\u2019s that celebrity doctor... Dr Litwak, Magus?\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cI told you, I\u2019m not in character. And time for a test. What monster was she in the mythic age?\u201d </i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cObviously vaccines hadn\u2019t been invented back then, so she couldn\u2019t have opposed anti-vaxxers. It would be something similar. Sick children\u2026 social status of medicine... some sort of demon who punished the wicked with plague. She gave people an excuse to banish the sick, you say disease only strikes sinners so you feel justified kicking them out to prevent contagion.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cFull marks. Question two, why don\u2019t we want her going after anti-vaxxers?\u201d </i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cCome on Greg, you ask that every time. Fear is the disease not the symptom. Scared people are irrational, especially about their kids. Scare people into using vaccines and they\u2019ll panic about something else. Will killing her really make people more rational?\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cNo. If you want to do that study medicine and minor in journalism, if you think kids should be protected from scared parents go into politics and make vaccines mandatory. Or don't, humanity will figure something out, it usually does. Our job is just to smooth over a few bumps on the road. Now\u201d he handed over a folder \u201cwe want a full excision from the mythscape. The Dreamwalkers have identified three Heroes on her tail. Third test, who shall we use, and how?\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <br /> When asked about their origins the Hunters of Llannerch Athrawon tell this story to their apprentices, it might even be true.<br /> <br /> In the hearts of all mankind dwell the archetypes, primordial ideas that humanity created to make sense of a confusing world. At the dawn of humanity the most powerful archetype was known by many names. The Shaman, The Priest, The Hermit, The Magician. The man who walked beyond the borders of the village to confront mankind\u2019s fears, to learn from the quest, and then to return as a teacher.<br /> <br /> As history progressed The Shaman was supplanted by The Hero. Like his predecessor the Hero would go to face fears, but he would slay them and return not to teach, but to bask in glory.<br /> <br /> However an Archetype as powerful as The Shamen is hard to erase, instead it transformed. The Shaman\u2019s existence began to revolve around The Hero, a stepping stone on The Hero\u2019s path to glory. Yet something unexpected happened. Freed from the need to teach, the Shaman\u2019s knowledge became ever more esoteric. Wisdom that anyone could learn became occult lore that ordinary men could not and did not want to comprehend.<br /> <br /> Llannerch Athrawon claim that their earliest founders were ancient wise men whose archetype caused them to realise that they were in fact vessels for a archetype from mankind\u2019s subconscious. These ancient wise men uncovered the secrets of the mythscape, they learned that their role was a side character in the Hero\u2019s story, and they decided to roll with it.<br /> <br /> <b>[Picture: A long bearded man wearing a robe and wizard hat flourishes an enormous scroll.] </b><br /> <br /> <b>Behold! I am Myrddin! </b><br /> <b>Keeper of the ancient scrolls!</b><br /> <b>Harken, Hero, to the prophecy and learn your destiny!</b><br /> <br /> Fast forward a few thousand years and you get to the modern Llannerch Athrawon. They may or may not be touched by fundamental human archetypes, but like all myths the literal truth is not the point. Llannerch Athrawon choose to act as though they are because the Heroes have been touched and playing to archetypes is the best way to direct the Hero\u2019s power before it\u2019s wasted on plans that would be sensible, would be morally acceptable, only if they were in a story.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Hunters</span><br /> You were always a power broker, an attach\u00e9 or nebulous assistant to politicians. You were the master of the back room deal, the urinal chat, the quid pro quo, but you weren't in it for power or money. You believed in the semi-technocratic, economic, and globalist ideals that governed the world. And when the markets crunched you saw educated people flocking to populist demagogues on the far left and far right. The question burned inside you. Why? Why was humanity so easily seduced by easy answers. The experts never predicted this, they couldn't explain it, so you called on every contact you had to find someone who could.<br /> <br /> When you were a child your brother was torn apart by a mob, accused of witchcraft. Your family fled to America and you spent your life becoming the anthesis of the ignorant superstitious mob that you escaped. In your studies you learned a lot about why people take up torches and pitchforks. The symbiosis between the Beasts who cultivate ignorance and superstition, and the Heroes who direct it. Once you wanted nothing more than to turn your back on the world you left behind but somebody has to be the hero, and if the Heroes can't do it that leaves you.<br /> <br /> As a teenager you dreamt of being swept off your feat by a blue eyed lantern jawed hero. A Beast decided to teach you that a woman should be strong and independent, and the lesson tore you in two. You're pushing thirty but half of you is still that wide eyed teen hoping for a strong hero to protect her from a vast and scary world. The other half is cynical, street smart, and psychologically incapable of forming an emotional connection to another human being. You can switch between your two halves at will, which is why Heroes will fight any foe for the chance to rescue you, and how you make sure the Heroes always win.<br /> <br /> In your youth you studied in the Towers of High Sorcery, received the blessings of Mystra, and dredged up forgotten lore from ancient ruins and vast caverns beneath the Earth. But you don't have time to play Dungeons &amp; Dragons these days, nor do you quest through dungeons or fight dragons in real life. That's the Heroes' job. But your days planning a quest through a dungeon taught you what you needed to plan a Hero's quest into a Lair, and knowing how to stay in charachter is vital if you want a Hero to stick to your plan.<br /> <br /> Who could predict that a show about colourful ponies making friends, having adventures, and working in harmony would be popular outside the pre-teen girl demographic? You could. You saw the signs in the mythscape, people were ready for a change from the ironic and the cynical, and you made sure your show was first to market, providing uplifting idealism with a large topping of teamwork and respect for society.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">The Enemy</span><br /> <br /> Llannerch Athrawon consider their prime enemy to the be the mythscape, the part of humanity\u2019s collective unconscious that contains primal ideas and archetypes. The order believes that something damaged the mythscape back in prehistory (though many suspect the \u201cdamage\u201d is a natural product of evolution creating the human mind piecemeal). Beasts, Heroes, and their own abilities are products of this damage; of course only the first two are a problem.<br /> <br /> Beasts are teachers, but they teach only through fear and according to Llannerch Athrawon that\u2019s the problem. Fear is the mindkiller, the enemy of rationality. Fear is all well and good for simple problems, fear of a tiger will keep you safe from the tiger. Fear of global warming will push you towards comforting rituals rather than the sweeping technological or sociological changes needed for a real solution. Fear of people outside your tribe might have valuable lessons but they\u2019re just not worth the costs.<br /> <br /> As for Heroes. Their tendency towards collateral damage would be bad enough, but as a subconscious archetype they represent selfish and violent solutions to problems. That belongs back in the bronze age.<br /> <br /> However the Compact has also realised that on the whole, whatever damage afflicts the mythscape, it\u2019s not that big of a deal. The damage happened back in the bronze age (or earlier) and it never stopped humanity advancing in the millennia since then. The true Llannerch Athrawon still try to fix the damage regardless. They are psychonauts exploring the collective unconscious for a solution and storytellers who try to manipulate humanity\u2019s mythology. Llannerch Athrawon realised a long time ago that trying to be a behind the scenes puppet master for all of fiction was a fool's errand, but their ranks contain master storytellers who can change the course of fiction with a single masterpiece, and of course, the inevitable legion of unaffiliated copycats.<br /> <br /> The rest of the Compact, the not-true Llannerch Athrawon, comprise the vast majority of the members. They just deal with the symptoms not the disease. They keep Heroes from causing collateral damage, they use Heroes to prune individual Beasts from the mythscape. It won\u2019t change the world, but a life saved is a life saved.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Stereotypes</span><br /> <br /> Ageis Kai Doru: Those assholes stole our bag of dream sand!<br /> <br /> Lucifuge: Heaven and hell are real enough all right. I've seen the proof with my own eyes. But Christianity, that's just a story people tell to each other, and I can't help but feel it's making you unhappy friend. Try reading this.<br /> <br /> Ride to Damascus: If it were as easy as putting the juju on a few Beasts we'd have fixed the mythscape already, but we know better than anyone not to trifle with someone carrying that kind of power... still, I wouldn't mind having that for myself.<br /> <br /> The Wilde Society: If you want to commission a true master of the written word speak to the Wilde Society. If you want to commission a professional who cares about deadlines or common courtesy speak to anyone else.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Archetypes</span><br /> <br /> Different members of Llannech Athrawon specialise in different techniques for manipulating Heroes.<br /> <br /> The most common role played by Llannerch Athrawon is <b>The Wizard</b>. They work behind the scenes manipulating Heroes to ensure their success, and when they interact directly it's through disguises or proxies.<br /> Free Specialty: Suberfuge (Long Cons)<br /> <br /> Known alternatively as <b>The Lover</b> or <b>The Lickspittle</b>, some hunters integrate themselves into a Hero's circle. As Heroes are archetypical characters themselves their relationship to people who resemble other archetypes has been codified long ago. The damsel who is constantly being rescued, the mysterious mentor who rarely answers questions, or da chief who chews out the Hero in an act of reverse psychology, Llannerch Athrawon have played them all.<br /> Free Specialty: Subterfuge (Staying in charachter)<br /> <br /> <b>The Visionary</b> remains true to Llannerch Atherwon's origonal mission, to understand and fix the mythscape. Visionaries quest through the Astral to try and discover what has damaged to humanity's psyche and how it might be fixed, or at least mitigated.<br /> Free Specialty: Occult (Astral)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Status </span><br /> <br /> Status in Llannerch Athrawon is an odd thing. Partly it exists as an informal grapevine between members, but mostly Status consists of acting like a wizard, at lest while you're &quot;on the clock&quot;. Guiding Heroes, enacting schemes, and even learning about the Occult all increase Status. The unusual training Llannerch Athrawon provides it's hunters gives them the ability to instinctively recognise each other, and how well they fulfil the Compact's mission.<br /> <br /> O Someone thought you had what it takes, and introduced you to Lightweaver in the astral realms. You passed the Archetype\u2019s test and were inducted into Llannerch Athrawon. Your training grants the Omen Sensitivity Merit, but ignore the Drawback. In addition you may study Lightweaving.<br /> <br /> OOO You\u2019ve done your job well and your name has started to spread among Llannerch Athrawon. Members of the Compact trust you enough to introduce you to their assets, and you\u2019re starting to build a network of your own. Take the Fixer Merit.<br /> <br /> OOOOO: As you reach the apex of Llannerch Athrawon the supernatural senses granted by the Compact's unique training grow. Take the Unseen Senses Merit applied to all supernatural phenomena. In addition, you can discern different types of supernatural phenomena. You could not tell that a Vampire actually is a Vampire, but you could tell two Vampires are the same kind of monster and if you identify one as a vampire you can identify Vampires from that point on.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Lightweaving (O - OOOOO)</span><br /> <br /> Llannerch Athrawon has historically had a problem. Drawing powers from occult archetypes has made them surprisingly good at finding Endowments. Being small and not well armed they have been vulnerable to larger Conspiracies stealing their Endowments; and then \u201cenforcing their copyright\u201d.<br /> <br /> They have good feelings about Lightweaving though. It can only be learned deep in the astral realms from an Archetype that nobody\u2019s heard of in a good fifteen centuries. He\u2019s referred to only as The Lightweaver to throw other Hunters off the scent; but as he dwells in the Archetypical realm shared by most Wizardly archetypes it\u2019s a dangerous place to make trouble; and Llannerch Athrawon has a lot of friends there.<br /> <br /> Most Weaves have a role; the hunter must be dressed and acting the part of the weave simply won\u2019t function. If someone sees through the disguise or the hunter breaks character they can no longer use Weaves that depend upon their role for the remainder of the scene - usually this means that they have almost no Weaves at all unless they can slip into a bathroom and quickly change disguises. Justifying the presence of a second wizard in the area can be a stretch, especially if people are already suspicious of a fake wizard, but a second policeman or some other common role is usually straight forward.<br /> <br /> <b>Agonise</b><br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Willpower<br /> <br /> Role: Any role which might plausibly have the chosen mundane or magical weapon<br /> <br /> Roll: Presence + Firearms or Weaponry<br /> <br /> The hunter creates a purely illusionary weapon. It cannot do damage, but it still hurts. A successful roll creates a weapon that lasts for one scene. Swords, pistols, rocket launchers or even plasma cannons or magic wands are all valid options - though the weapon's Damage cannot exceed the Hunter's dots in Lightweaving.<br /> <br /> Track illusionary damage as normal, but remove it at the end of the scene. Supernatraul powers that defend against mental influence can provide Armour against illusionary damage and illusionary damage can be cured by both normal methods or countermagic. Unnecessary stitches or other consequences are of course fully real.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>All A Dream</b><br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Willpower<br /> <br /> Role: A therapist, a police man, or some other authority figure who's supposed to explain what happened.<br /> <br /> Roll: Manipulation + Empathy<br /> <br /> Beasts don't remain in their lairs but go forth and feast. Heroes grandstand and pay little attention to collateral damage. Both draw in bystanders, witnesses and authorities whose involvement might threaten a hunter's delicate plan. So the Llannerch Athrawon find ways to distract them, or when they're feeling generous to help put people back together after a Beast terrorised them for it's own amusement.<br /> <br /> All a Dream is a very intricate piece of illusionism, Lightweaving cannot affect your memories, but it can create an auditory illusion that sounds like your own thoughts or a visual illusion directly on the eyeball that looks just like a memory. Done properly, to a person in the right psychological state, Llannerch Athrawon can convince people that a Beast's Nightmare was just an ordinary nightmare or that the Hero was horrified by the car crash - not bragging that the Beast died in the collision. The ethics of this practice are debatable (especially since mindgames can go horribly wrong), the effectiveness is not.<br /> <br /> All a Dream can only be invoked on a character who recently Failed or Dramatically Failed a Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The hunter only convinces his target that whatever authority he represents is part of a conspiracy dedicated to hushing up the supernatural truth.<br /> <br /> Failure: The hunter just sounds implausible, as this is the world of Darkness the mortal may still decide to keep quiet but the damage remains.<br /> <br /> Success: The effects of a recent breaking point caused by exposure to or an attack by the supernatural vanish and the target believes the hunter\u2019s story. This may even restore a lost dot of Integrity.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: As above, and the Hunter gains a positive condition. The mortal may open up and provide Informed or offer a favour at some point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Bleaching the Grey</b><br /> <br /> Cost: 1+ Willpower<br /> <br /> Role: None<br /> <br /> Dicepool: Manipulation + Lightweaving<br /> <br /> A simple Weave, Bleaching the Grey creates a dead body. While originally invented by a member of Llannerch Athrawon to fake his own death hunters have found that there's no ends of practical uses for a dead body.<br /> <br /> The body created can appear to have died of any cause the hunter wishes and reacts naturally to post-mortem trauma; which allows for tricks like creating a body that died of untraceable poisons then shooting it with your enemy's gun.<br /> <br /> Surface examination will never reveal the ruse, though a bizarre or implausible death may still attract suspicion. Medical examination, a perception roll by a creature with superhuman senses, or magical examination may uncover the truth if they roll higher than the Hunter's successes.<br /> <br /> The corpse created lasts for Lightweaving * Willpower spent days.<br /> <br /> <b>Crystal Ball</b><br /> <br /> Cost 1 Willopwer<br /> <br /> Role: Wits + Science (potentially opposed by magical defences)<br /> <br /> One of the simplest but most useful weaves, Crystal Ball creates an auditory and visual illusion of another place and time. Be it what's happening right now on the other side of that wall or what happened in the Hero's home the night he became a Hero. The hunter must know the exact distance between herself and her target, taking into account the movement and curvature of the Earth. Over short distances or anywhere the hunter can see with their own eye (including with binoculars or telescopes) this is automatic, for longer distances LLannerch Athrawon simply hired a few programmers and can get the numbers by typing in the GPS and date they wish to see into their phones.<br /> <br /> In game terms, the player may ask the Storyteller one question per success rolled, which he must answer (within reason).<br /> <br /> <b>Dreamwalking</b><br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Willpower<br /> <br /> Role: A shaman or a similar practitioner able to commune with other worlds<br /> <br /> Dicepool: Wits + Lightweaving<br /> <br /> Any mortal can in theory reach the Astral world, but it takes decades of training. Consequently whenever they have an Endowment one of the first things Llannerch Athrawon do is try and find an easier way in. Fortunately Lightweaving provides.<br /> <br /> Dreamwalking (also known as Holodecking) creates a full five sensory illusion of the Astral realms. For some reason this in turn allows Astral beings to perceive the hunter, Llannerch Athrawon don't know why but they aren't going to look a gift horse in the mouth.<br /> <br /> In short, Dreamwalking provides quick and easy access to the Astral Realms, without years of training or meditation.<br /> <br /> Originally Llannerch Athrawon would Dreamwalk in empty flat fields, walking in the Astral requires them to walk in the real world, but recently they've found a better way than fulfilling the old stereotypes of mad ecstatic shamans. It turns out they didn't need to walk, just move their legs in a walking like fashion. Now, so long as they have the necessary equipment, the hunters suspend themselves in mid air where they can wave their limbs without moving and in complete privacy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mask of Many Faces</b><br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Willpower<br /> <br /> Role: None<br /> <br /> Dicepool: Manipulation + Lightweaving<br /> <br /> The most common weave, Mask of Many Faces allows the hunters of Llannerch Athrawon to disguise themselves as just about anything of the same Size and general shape. Usually this means as a person or as an inconspicuous inanimate object.<br /> <br /> The illusions are powerful and cover all five senses. With this weave a large (but not Giant) man could convincingly pass himself off as a demure woman (or vise versa). Indeed, Llannerch Athrawon has long known that most Heroes dream of rescuing a prince or princess depending on their tastes and quite a few won\u2019t let their own sex bar them from such a useful method of persuasion.<br /> <br /> When disguised as a person the hunter only needs to make a subterfuge roll if they break character or someone has a good reason to be suspicious. While disguised as a police officer everyone will believe they are an officer of the law unless they have a good reason not too. Disguising yourself as a specific person usually requires Subterfuge rolls when interacting with people who know them. If a Subterfuge roll is made add Lightweaving to your dicepool.<br /> <br /> Disguising yourself as an inanimate object provides Lightweaving automatic successes for Stealth, so long as you\u2019re acting like an inanimate object. Mask of Many Faces won\u2019t help if people see a tree start walking. Recolouring yourself as a camouflage pattern and similar tricks simply adds Lightweaving to your Stealth dice pool for the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Perseus\u2019 Shield</b><br /> <br /> Role: Someone who can create or is likely to possess magical artifacts.<br /> <br /> Roll: Manipulation + Subterfuge vs Composure + Empathy or Subterfuge<br /> <br /> Llannerch Athrawon say that the story of Perseus and Medusa is an half accurate retelling of a historical battle between a Hero and a Beast. When Llannerch Athrawon found Perseus he was halfway to inflicting an Anathema upon Medusa, one which would make her so ugly that any man or woman would flee from her; after this was done he intended to take an ordinary sword and fight a monster who did not in fact have any weaknesses.<br /> <br /> In response a hunter of Llannerch Athrawon disguised himself as the goddess Athena and gave Perseus a mirrored shield which would protect him from Medusa's Nightmares. The mirrored shield was in fact perfectly ordinary shield with a cheap trick (no matter what Endowment they're using at the time, Llannerch Athrawon find some way to use it to create Perseus' Shield) to make it reflective and look like a powerful artifact. It was Perseus' belief that turned the shield into an Anathema.<br /> <br /> In short, if the hunter beats the Hero in a contested role they can choose which Anathema the hero will create. Since the Hunters of Llannerch Athrawon are sane and actually understand how Anathema work their choices are usually superior.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wizard\u2019s Weapon</b><br /> <br /> Role: None.<br /> <br /> Dicepool: N/A<br /> <br /> When taking this ability the hunter gains one weapon of a size equal or less than Lightweaving that is permanently disguised as an equally sized mundane and harmless object. If combined with Mask of Many Faces the disguise will adapt to every mask. For example a shotgun could be disguised as a large staff while acting as a wizard, an ordinary shotgun while disguised as a farmer, but shift into an umbrella when the hunter changes into a businessman.<br /> <br /> Wizard's Weapon does not provide a gun, the Hunter must provide their own weapon.<br /> <br /> Guns and similar items also disguise their ammunition, that shotgun disguised a staff could disguise both the sight and sound of firing as a lightning bolt.<br /> <br /> Apart from being able to travel in public with a weapon, when the weapon is disguised as a supernatural object attacking mortals with &quot;magic&quot; triggers a breaking point, as would any form of supernatural attack. The hunters or Llannerch Athrawon aren\u2019t particularly great in combat, but throwing a lightning bolt can quickly sow panic in their foes. It\u2019s a good way to clear out a monster\u2019s cultists without the Hero having to kill them, or to scare off a couple of muggers without having to get into a real fight.<br /> <br /> Trying to use the weapon outside an appropriate role will break the illusion, though a shotgun disguised as an umbrella can still be extreemly useful even if you only get one shot before you break the illusion (along with your Mask of Many Faces).<br /> <br /> <b>Wizard's Rune of Destruction</b><br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Willpower<br /> <br /> Role: Anyone who could have access to supernatural objects.<br /> <br /> Dicepool: Manipulation + Lightweaving<br /> <br /> This weave is a variant on Wizard's Weapon. It lacks the ability to create a permanent illusion but it may be used on any weapon or trap the Hunter wishes instead of a single signature item. The illusions created last one scene<br /> <br /> Because this weave doesn't provide any method for carrying a weapon in public, it is mostly used for improvised weapons and traps, or even accidents if they see it coming with enough time to weave an illusion. <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-09-2017, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T05:33:35-07:00","id":571227,"title":"","content":"So the usual second post commentry.<br /> <br /> Llannerch Athrawon (Rough translation: Mentor's Glade, yes their name is a place) started off as an idea back when Beasts was just spoilers. If there was Heroes than obviously there would be room for Gandalf. The fact Heroes were both insane and antagonists just made it work even better - and I had the rough sketch waiting for the Kickstarter preview so I could see how Hero powers work and work that into the Endowment (see <b>Perseus\u2019 Shield</b>). However reading the kickstarter document made me loose interest. Basically I agreed with the common criticisms; and at risk of this thread derailing I shan't say any more on this topic.<br /> <br /> In the end the revisions made me change my mind again. The idea of Beasts teaching through fear - and before I continue I want to say this next bit is <b>strictly </b>from an <b>in charachter</b> perspective - struck me as such a bad idea that I just had to write a rebuttal. Llannerch Athrawon is that rebuttal, the intro fiction makes it explicit; and that's the most of my politics that's ever ended up in my writing. Hopefully it remains the most political I get, I mean, I did manage to write Princess: the Hopeful without letting my own politics in <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> One thing I am disapointed at is the Status Merit. In retrospect it ends up saying that their Archetype theory is correct; but I had to justify Omen Sensitivity somehow. It's key to the whole wizard concept. On the other hand I really like how the Dreamwalking power turned out with the suspension ropes. It's like seing a film set and seeing that there's no roof. It doesn't make it a lie, but it shows that it's... not fake, but fictional. Fictional is good word for Llannerch Athrawon.<br /> <br /> <br /> Fun fact. Both Stephenie Meyer and George R. R. Martin are members of the compact. Between Twilight and Song of Fire and Ice a generation of copycat storytellers are writing without a classical hero. Edward is a red herring, he's that way to sell books, the real plot is to push the urban fantasy genera from one of heroes and quests towards one of romance. I thought about making that cannon but decided it was a step too far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-28-2015, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T06:06:08-07:00","id":571236,"title":"","content":"nice concept, and it gives me an immediate character concept who use Tarot card archetypes as a tools for them as guides in the &quot;Hero's Journey&quot;. Now I only wonder where I should put them on my Hunter map :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T09:56:49-07:00","id":571596,"title":"","content":"I think you should and more powers related to the manipulation of the Hero and their abilities, not only illusionism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T07:46:22-07:00","id":572631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero?p=571596#post571596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you should and more powers related to the manipulation of the Hero and their abilities, not only illusionism.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Beast is about messing with the roles in mythical structures, then it would make sense for this compact to do so as well. And one way to do that would be for the magic to be in the hands of the Heroes, and what the compact does be limited to &quot;extreme psychology&quot; (inlcuding psychic driving); I'd even advocate cutting lightweaving, instead being generous with allowing mortal-only supernatural merits. Of course colder members of the compact could follow the philosophy of a more recent example of the hero's mentor, the Watchers' Council of Buffy: that the <i>Heroes</i> are their Endowment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero?p=571227#post571227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of Beasts teaching through fear - and before I continue I want to say this next bit is strictly from an in charachter perspective - struck me as such a bad idea that I just had to write a rebuttal.</div> </div> </div> </div>One line in the revised intro (or maybe chapter 2, I dont have time to check right now) says that to learn from a nightmare, you have to wake from it. There <i>are</i> useful lessons to learn from fear, but they aren't learned <i>while you're afraid</i> - they come after, when you calm down and integrate your experience into the rest of your life. Some Beasts get that, some don't - it would make sense for some members of the compact to get it and some not as well.<br /> <br /> Sadly, though, I'm not a fan of this compact; they seem better suited to the Diskworld than the World of Darkness. (Not meant as an insult, the Diskworld rocks, but in the same way that nails aren't screws...).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T11:09:22-07:00","id":572928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero?p=572631#post572631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Beast is about messing with the roles in mythical structures, then it would make sense for this compact to do so as well. And one way to do that would be for the magic to be in the hands of the Heroes, and what the compact does be limited to &quot;extreme psychology&quot; (inlcuding psychic driving); I'd even advocate cutting lightweaving, instead being generous with allowing mortal-only supernatural merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lightweaving lets you cut out a lot of the filler and get to the meat of extreme psychology. Want to show a Hero their little sister's corpse in the wreckage of their own bomb. You could bribe mortuary workers and plastic surgeons, or you could skip past that with a quick illusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero?p=572631#post572631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There <i>are</i> useful lessons to learn from fear, but they aren't learned <i>while you're afraid</i> - they come after, when you calm down and integrate your experience into the rest of your life.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't fix anything. The amount of life lessons that are<br /> <br /> 1) Important enough to justify a Nightmare.<br /> 2) Simple enough to teach through fear.<br /> 3) Has an easily identifiable group of people who need to learn the lesson.*<br /> 4) Who won't learn it without a Beast's personal touch.<br /> <br /> Is starting to approach zero.<br /> <br /> <br /> * To Clarify. Lets say your lesson is &quot;don't talk to strangers or you might get hurt.&quot; Then unless you only terrorise people who were going to get hurt by a stranger you're a net negative on their life. You need some way of identifying students.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero?p=572631#post572631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it would make sense for some members of the compact to get it and some not as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Compact gets it, that's why they think the whole idea is bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero?p=572631#post572631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, though, I'm not a fan of this compact; they seem better suited to the Diskworld than the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div> How so? They're not that different to a Guardian of the Veil Labythnth that focuses on Heroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-29-2015, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T14:04:11-07:00","id":573139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd even advocate cutting lightweaving, instead being generous with allowing mortal-only supernatural merits. Of course colder members of the compact could follow the philosophy of a more recent example of the hero's mentor, the Watchers' Council of Buffy: that the <i>Heroes</i> are their Endowment. </div> </div> </div>Errr... most Watchers actually had some competency in magic, including alchemy, protective wards and even demonology. Giles was far from being the exception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T14:20:22-07:00","id":573154,"title":"","content":"And that's just the Watchers. Gandalf, Merlin, Obi-Wan Kenobi and others who mentor the Hero have a lot of magic (or the Force).<br /> <br /> One of the concepts behind illusions is that it's a good way to make them <i>look like</i> they have Gandalf quality magic without wondering why they don't just zap the Beast themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T14:32:15-07:00","id":573183,"title":"","content":"I think that illusions thematically work for that group. It both works around the idea of them as the ones who work behind the scenes instead of leading the plot, and it connects them to the Nightmares Beasts can use- that is, a similar power from a different source. They are there to make sure the story would go the right way- with the right Hero killing the right Beast in the right time in the right way. Subtle abilities which influence the &quot;characters in the myth&quot; without directly interfering (like illusions) seem like a good Endowment to them, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T16:55:13-07:00","id":573317,"title":"","content":"These guys seem like they might work as a good villain for a Beast game. Really liking Lightweaving; do they get access to all the powers with the first dot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T00:23:47-07:00","id":573641,"title":"","content":"No. They get one power per dot for free; and then they must buy extra powers with experience points. Same as Benediction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T02:44:45-07:00","id":573685,"title":"","content":"Regarding the &quot;attire &quot; and perfomance necessary for the lightweaving, must it be obvious and flamboyan, Gandalf or Dumbledore style, or can be more modern and subtle like Harry Dresden?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 06-30-2015, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T06:41:55-07:00","id":573875,"title":"","content":"I imagine harry dresden style is fine for the default, but that as actors they'll play up to their audience- If they need to go full Gandolf route to get a hero's attention, they'll go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T10:25:36-07:00","id":574084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero?p=573685#post573685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the &quot;attire &quot; and perfomance necessary for the lightweaving, must it be obvious and flamboyan, Gandalf or Dumbledore style, or can be more modern and subtle like Harry Dresden?</div> </div> </div> </div> The answer is whatever the audience will accept. If a Hero was a comic book fan and recognizes the trenchcoat brigadier look then that's fine. However if their only exposure to fantasy is major summer blockbusters then robes it is.<br /> <br /> Don't forget you can change roles easily. You could wear the full Gandalf look when you first meet the hero; tell them the prophecy says they'll find the magic sword in a museum. Then disguise yourself as far more subtle professor at the museum, help him find the magic sword and integrate yourself into his entourage in a more low key role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-30-2015, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T04:11:56-07:00","id":578551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero?p=572928#post572928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't fix anything. The amount of life lessons that are<br /> ...<br /> Is starting to approach zero.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, even in your example, I'd be sympathetic to the idea that an anti-vaxxer really needs a terrifying reminder of what the diseases these vaccines are against are really like (and a reminder where no one actually gets sick and dies is preferable).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How so? They're not that different to a Guardian of the Veil Labythnth that focuses on Heroes. </div> </div> </div>Mm, an organisation of professional Gandalfs just seems goofy to me outside a comedic setting. I'll leave it there because I don't want to crap on it too much.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T04:47:22-07:00","id":578576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero?p=578551#post578551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, even in your example, I'd be sympathetic to the idea that an anti-vaxxer really needs a terrifying reminder of what the diseases these vaccines are against are really like (and a reminder where no one actually gets sick and dies is preferable).</div> </div> </div> </div> I have to disagree.<br /> <br /> From an ethical perspective if you can justify scaring an anti-vaxxer half to death; you can justify just giving their kids an injection behind their back. The moral principle behind anti-vaxx is a parents right to decide what's best for their children and the general right to refuse medical treatment. Once you've decided their views about vaccinees justify taking away that right, you have to think about the least harmful way to do that. Scaring them half to death until they consent is more harmful than just giving the shots.<br /> <br /> From a practical perspective anti-vax is the symptom not the disease. The disease is that humans like to feel in control; be it natural disasters or genetics, if it's uncontrollable we'll find some way to pretend it's not (usually religion). You can't teach people to accept their powerlessness through scaring them because; you're trying to teach them not to be afraid by using fear, it's not going to work.<br /> <br /> You scare them into using vaccines and they'll find some other ritual to ward off autism; feeling in control is a human need. Now maybe the next ritual will be less harmful; but governments are already coming up with more ethical ways to make people use vaccines than scaring them half to death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero?p=578551#post578551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mm, an organisation of professional Gandalfs just seems goofy to me outside a comedic setting. I'll leave it there because I don't want to crap on it too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually am interested in why you think it's goofy. Manipulator types are very common in the WoD. 2E Oribamus are mentioned to ocasionally go for the Gandalf look. Heroes are easily manipulated by playing Gandalf.<br /> <br /> It seems like it fits right into the WoD to me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T06:53:20-07:00","id":578686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero?p=578576#post578576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually am interested in why you think it's goofy. Manipulator types are very common in the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it's tainted because I can't get the image out of my head of what it would be like with <i>real</i> destinies and chosen ones - like a research department desperately trying to find out which of the two-dozen current looming dooms, known prophecies, and rising dark lords go with which of the thirty plus people they have on file with signs indicating they might be chosen - because no one wants a debacle like the time Ar'tydea was devastated by undead because they'd mistakenly sent the champion destined to kill the resurgent dragon Kardax against the Lich-King (not to mention figuring out what the hell they'll do when Kardax really does resurge). Try as I might, I can't unsee this when I look at this compact, which means I can't take it seriously - through no fault of your own.<br /> <br /> More uncharitably, when a compact is written from an anti-the-central-idea-of-Beast slant, I'm also led to look at it via the critical-of-Beast view of Heroes, from which perspective this compact is using mentally broken catspaws to prosecute a fight they're quite capable of undertaking themselves, instead of manipulating them into therapy where they might end up more functional.<br /> <br /> (This is ironic in that I'm not overfond of the teaching thing either, though I don't particularly dislike it either; in my setting, it'll just be something a lot of Beasts buy into in order to live with themselves).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T07:12:16-07:00","id":578693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero?p=578686#post578686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More uncharitably, when a compact is written from an anti-the-central-idea-of-Beast slant, I'm also led to look at it via the critical-of-Beast view of Heroes, from which perspective this compact is using mentally broken catspaws to prosecute a fight they're quite capable of undertaking themselves, instead of manipulating them into therapy where they might end up more functional.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which means they fit right in with the torturers, vivisectionists, drug dealers, blackmailers, terrorists, serial killers, and cannibals one can already find among hunters. <br /> <br /> At what point hunters stop having any moral superiority over their foes is a built in point of the game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T08:41:52-07:00","id":578801,"title":"","content":"I see it as Grey vs Gray Morality. The Beasts are a problem, no matter how they may justify their existence and predations over humanity. They are also the reason Heroes exist. Llannerch cannot cure Heroes from what they are, neither have the power to take down Beasts on their own. So the beast they can do from their perspective is to coach the first against the second ones aka Let's You And You Fight.. and try to prevent as much collateral damage as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 07-04-2015, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T09:21:30-07:00","id":578866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero?p=578686#post578686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose it's tainted because I can't get the image out of my head of what it would be like with <i>real</i> destinies and chosen ones - like a research department desperately trying to find out which of the two-dozen current looming dooms, known prophecies, and rising dark lords go with which of the thirty plus people they have on file with signs indicating they might be chosen - because no one wants a debacle like the time Ar'tydea was devastated by undead because they'd mistakenly sent the champion destined to kill the resurgent dragon Kardax against the Lich-King (not to mention figuring out what the hell they'll do when Kardax really does resurge). Try as I might, I can't unsee this when I look at this compact, which means I can't take it seriously - through no fault of your own.</div> </div> </div> </div> Um. What's goofy about that? I'm being serious. It sounds awesome.<br /> <br /> Actually, that's basically the plot of the 500 Kingdoms series; the half that isn't a romance novel. I quite enjoyed that half.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero?p=578686#post578686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More uncharitably, when a compact is written from an anti-the-central-idea-of-Beast slant, I'm also led to look at it via the critical-of-Beast view of Heroes, from which perspective this compact is using mentally broken catspaws to prosecute a fight they're quite capable of undertaking themselves, instead of manipulating them into therapy where they might end up more functional.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call this &quot;goofy&quot; but it i's a completely valid criticism of their methods. IMO Llannerch are correct about Beasts, but that doesn't automatically make them nice people.<br /> <br /> How nesscary Heroes are to the mission, I.E. if a Hero killing a Beast affects the Primodrial Dream in a way other methods don't; is something I'm leaving up to individual Storytellers. Though if Heroes aren't special like that (and you don't make Gifts way more powerful), you have to come up with some other justification for why they don't have a better method.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero?p=578693#post578693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which means they fit right in with the torturers, vivisectionists, drug dealers, blackmailers, terrorists, serial killers, and cannibals one can already find among hunters.<br /> <br /> At what point hunters stop having any moral superiority over their foes is a built in point of the game</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed it is one of the driving questions; though personally I think the question doesn't apply when you're hunting something like Infernal Demons - even the worst Hunters are better than the best Infernals. Beasts... eh they're probably closer to Grey than to Black despite the impression the book gives me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-05-2015, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T05:41:27-07:00","id":580839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero?p=578866#post578866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't call this &quot;goofy&quot; but it i's a completely valid criticism of their methods. IMO Llannerch are correct about Beasts, but that doesn't automatically make them nice people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well this part I didn't find goofy, I found it repugnant. But if that's intended as a valid reading of them, then I withdraw it as a criticism.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T15:53:38-07:00","id":583947,"title":"","content":"In the interests of full disclosure - I didn't intend one way or the other. I came up with the concept of a Gandalf group and just wrote what came into my head. But when I read your view it seemed like a perfectly sensible reading.<br /> <br /> The only things I really intended were:<ul><li>Their primary MO is manipulating heroes and well, being generally manipulative and scheming.</li> <li>They on occasion look and act like Gandalf.</li> <li>They had a rebuttal to the idea of teaching through fear.</li> <li>They're competent. (I always have this one. I'm not interested in playing an incompetent Hunter)</li> </ul><br /> So providing you give them a reason to manipulate heroes that's correct and sensible enough that it doesn't make them incompetent it's compatible with my authorial intent. I get the impression that modifying Hero Gifts so that they're significantly better at fighting Beasts than guns or Lightweaving and making that the reason they use Hero pawns would not address your moral revulsion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T13:16:02-07:00","id":640584,"title":"","content":"I've added a new weave - crystal ball.<br /> <br /> You may be wondering why it has that stuff about the movement and curvature of the Earth. It's for thematics. To highlight the point that are <i>not</i> wizards they just act the part. Thus Crystal Ball pointedly uses scientific measures of distance rather than magical measures like sympathetic connections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T14:39:06-07:00","id":640660,"title":"","content":"Err... using scientific measures would make sense if they were invoking Clarke Third, which they aren\u00b4t: their powers come from a archetype from the Dreaming, thus they count as <i>magical </i>as Disciplines or Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T23:39:25-07:00","id":641214,"title":"","content":"I'd say the Dreaming is closer to psychic phenomina than magic. Certainly as the sum of all mankind's knowledge and experiences it will lean towards scientific understanding rather than magical understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-27-2015, 03:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T07:52:02-07:00","id":641549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero?p=641214#post641214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say the Dreaming is closer to psychic phenomina than magic. Certainly as the sum of all mankind's knowledge and experiences it will lean towards scientific understanding rather than magical understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm... guess that? I think you have just given me an inspiration about the concept of the Maelstrom for the next time I play Apocalypse World. Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T03:30:33-07:00","id":643918,"title":"","content":"This doesn't feel like a compact; putting aside the fact it has an Endowment it feels too high concept &amp; <i>conspiratorial. </i>Manipulating Heroes and covertly sabotaging primordial nightmares, playing the power behind the throne and the trickster...<br /> They are so tier 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T06:25:34-07:00","id":644029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero?p=643918#post643918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't feel like a compact; putting aside the fact it has an Endowment it feels too high concept &amp; <i>conspiratorial. </i>Manipulating Heroes and covertly sabotaging primordial nightmares, playing the power behind the throne and the trickster...<br /> They are so tier 3.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The key is <i>pretending </i>to be powerful, mystically and otherwise, to convince others to follow their schemes. In truth, they are not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;<i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Llannerch Athrawon has historically had a problem. Drawing powers from occult archetypes has made them surprisingly good at finding Endowments. <u><b>Being small and not well armed they have been vulnerable to larger Conspiracies</b></u> stealing their Endowments; and then \u201cenforcing their copyright\u201d.</span></span></span> </i> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T08:30:50-07:00","id":644171,"title":"","content":"Yes, I understand that is part of their deal; but just because time has not been kind doesn't change the fact they don't operate at a compact scale. The Lucifuge isn't exactly an overwhelming force (unlike say TF:V or MM) due to limited numbers and poor reputation but they get by. Llannerch feels like it could easily work in similar fashion. And lets not forget the next couple of lines either...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They have good feelings about Lightweaving though. It can only be learned deep in the astral realms from an Archetype that nobody\u2019s heard of in a good fifteen centuries. He\u2019s referred to only as The Lightweaver to throw<i><u><b> other Conspiracies </b></u></i>off the scent; </div> </div> </div>I get the impression that LA is at the threshold of the Compact/Conspiracy threshold. It lacks the manpower but it compensates with shenanigans like any wizard-trickster mentor should. I am really interested what the stereotypes for Conspiracies seeing as how the Llannerch has managed to get 'magic mugged' by them; safe to say they won't be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T13:53:30-07:00","id":644608,"title":"","content":"I have to disagree with them being a Conspiracy for a simple reason. Heroes and their team are nearly always Tier 1. Thus a Tier 2 group could easily manipulate them. The only other people they routinely manipulate is the sci-fi/fantay market and that's not exactly hard to do. Scope out the zeitgeist in the astral. Use that to get one of the authors in the Compact to write a best selling fantasy novel with no classic heroes, wait for the copycats to follow his lead. Also, they have a bottom up not a top down organisation.<br /> <br /> <br /> You wished for some stereotypes<br /> <br /> Aegis Kai Doru: They killed a dozen of our best to steal that pouch of dream sand, it was an amazing thing. One pinch and a hero would fall into a dream under our control, we could convince them of anything, give them any plan, and all before the sun rose. The pouch was infinite too, each of us could take all the sand we wanted. I still wonder who stole it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-21-2017, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}